note run-time pools, host refusal (run under prlimit --as=268435456): enlarge asks for 1 GiB, the host refuses
note (-12, ENOMEM); the pool is unchanged and the program goes on: a smaller enlarge then succeeds
global P uchar *
fn main to int
r = enlarge P 1073741824
if ne len P 0
ret 1
end
s = enlarge P 4096
if ne s 0
ret 2
end
put P 4095 9
ret int sub long 0 r
end
